From: Ezra Kruger <ekruges@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 01:32:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] ipc: emit window::move events for floating repositions

Floating containers repositioned via commands, drags, or output changes
never emitted window::move, so IPC consumers had to poll geometry.
Emit the event from floating_reposition(), matching what move.c does
for tiling moves.
---
 src/floating.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/floating.c b/src/floating.c
index d6f3682d..4bf778ec 100644
--- a/src/floating.c
+++ b/src/floating.c
@@ -769,6 +769,10 @@ bool floating_reposition(Con *con, Rect newrect) {
     }
 
     tree_render();
+
+    /* Repositioning a floating container is a move; tell IPC subscribers,
+     * matching what move.c does for tiling moves. */
+    ipc_send_window_event("move", con_descend_focused(con));
     return true;
 }
 
